---
import '../styles/global.css'
import archivoFont from '../assets/fonts/archivo-400_800-normal.woff2'
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`
const site = 'https://jomko.github.io/ginger-tail/'
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#171614" />
    <meta name="description" content="Meet Ginger Tail: an open-source Node.js runtime that carries useful context between temporary model calls, so a character can persist." />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Ginger Tail — The tail wags the cat." />
    <meta property="og:description" content="The model thinks. The cat stays. Ginger Tail carries useful context between calls." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://jomko.github.io/ginger-tail/og.jpg" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="RYZHYI, a mechanical ginger cat beside the words The Tail Wags the Cat." />
    <meta property="og:url" content={site} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Ginger Tail — The tail wags the cat." />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="The model thinks. The cat stays. Ginger Tail carries useful context between calls." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://jomko.github.io/ginger-tail/og.jpg" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={site} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}favicon.png`} type="image/png" sizes="32x32" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href={`${base}apple-touch-icon.png`} sizes="180x180" />
    <link rel="preload" href={archivoFont} as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <title>Ginger Tail — The tail wags the cat.</title>
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"SoftwareSourceCode","name":"Ginger Tail","codeRepository":"https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail","programmingLanguage":"JavaScript","description":"A local-first Node.js runtime foundation for long-lived AI agents."}</script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to the story</a>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#chapter-01"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">gt.</span><span>Ginger Tail</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Story chapters">
        <a href="#chapter-01">01 <span>Start</span></a>
        <a href="#chapter-02">02 <span>Meet</span></a>
        <a href="#chapter-03">03 <span>Yesterday</span></a>
        <a href="#chapter-04">04 <span>Get it</span></a>
      </nav>
      <a class="header-source" href="https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></a>
      <span class="reading-line" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>
    </header>
    <main id="main">
      <section class="chapter opener" id="chapter-01" aria-labelledby="opening-title">
        <div class="chapter-index"><span>01 / A small engine for agents with a past</span><span>Local-first · Node.js · MIT</span></div>
        <div class="opening-grid">
          <div class="opening-copy">
            <p class="overline"><span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Meet Ginger Tail</p>
            <h1 id="opening-title"><span>The tail</span><em>wags the cat.</em></h1>
            <p class="opening-dek">A brain is rented by the minute. <br />A life takes longer.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="#chapter-02"><span>Meet the three</span><span class="link-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          </div>
          <figure class="hero-cat">
            <img src={`${base}ryzhyi.webp`} alt="RYZHYI, a ginger mechanical cat with a segmented body, four paws and a tall fluffy tail" width="1748" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" />
          </figure>
        </div>
        <div class="opening-foot"><span>MODEL CALLS END.</span><span>THE CAT DOESN'T.</span><span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter cast" id="chapter-02" aria-labelledby="cast-title">
        <div class="chapter-index"><span>02 / Meet the three</span><span>Separate the thought from the life</span></div>
        <div class="cast-heading">
          <h2 id="cast-title">Three things.<br /><span>One remembered life.</span></h2>
          <p>The model is a visitor. The cat is who stays. Ginger Tail keeps the useful bits moving between calls.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cast-composition">
          <div class="cast-select" role="group" aria-label="Choose a layer to inspect">
            <button class="layer-button" type="button" data-layer="llm" aria-pressed="true"><span class="layer-number">01</span><span class="layer-title">The LLM</span><span class="layer-hint">Temporary intelligence</span><span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></button>
            <button class="layer-button" type="button" data-layer="cat" aria-pressed="false"><span class="layer-number">02</span><span class="layer-title">The cat</span><span class="layer-hint">Persistent character</span><span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></button>
            <button class="layer-button" type="button" data-layer="tail" aria-pressed="false"><span class="layer-number">03</span><span class="layer-title">Ginger Tail</span><span class="layer-hint">Continuity machinery</span><span class="layer-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></button>
          </div>
          <div class="layer-readout" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
            <p class="readout-label"><span class="readout-index">01</span><span class="readout-kicker">Temporary intelligence</span></p>
            <h3 class="readout-title">The call ends.<br />The thinking stops.</h3>
            <p class="readout-copy">A model reasons over the context a host gives it, then returns a proposal. It does not own the character, its diary, or the keys.</p>
            <p class="readout-fact"><span>OWNS</span><strong>One temporary turn</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter yesterday" id="chapter-03" aria-labelledby="yesterday-title">
        <div class="chapter-index"><span>03 / Yesterday matters</span><span>One cat · two mornings · two model calls</span></div>
        <div class="story-heading">
          <div><p class="overline">One cat. Two mornings. Two model calls.</p><h2 id="yesterday-title">Yesterday<br /><span>stays.</span></h2></div>
          <p>Scroll through one quiet day, one saved observation, and a new call that can begin with yesterday in reach.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-story">
          <div class="story-stage" role="group" data-scene="morning" aria-label="Illustrated story scene">
            <div class="stage-art">
              <img class="stage-room stage-room-day" src={`${base}yesterday-day.webp`} alt="" width="1639" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <img class="stage-room stage-room-night" src={`${base}yesterday-night.webp`} alt="" width="1639" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <img class="stage-room stage-room-dawn" src={`${base}yesterday-dawn.webp`} alt="" width="1639" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <span class="stage-contact-shadow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <img class="stage-cat" src={`${base}ryzhyi-layer.webp`} alt="" width="1639" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <img class="stage-bird" src={`${base}window-bird.webp`} alt="" width="1375" height="1144" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <span class="stage-model-light" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="stage-memory-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span class="stage-memory-link" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div class="stage-callout stage-callout-model" aria-hidden="true"><span>SCRIPTED MODEL CALL · NO LIVE LLM</span><strong>A bird at the window.</strong></div>
              <div class="stage-callout stage-callout-memory" aria-hidden="true"><span>SAVED · HOST MEMORY</span><strong>Bird at the window.</strong><small>Source: world/window/bird-01</small></div>
              <div class="stage-callout stage-callout-return" aria-hidden="true"><span>DIFFERENT CALL · SAME CAT</span><div><p><b>YESTERDAY</b>Bird at the window.</p><i aria-hidden="true">→</i><p><b>TODAY</b>The bird returns.</p></div><small>Host supplies the saved observation to this new call.</small></div>
            </div>
            <p class="stage-caption" aria-hidden="true"><span>ONE CAT</span><span>CONTINUING HISTORY</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="story-steps" aria-label="The story of two mornings">
            <article class="story-step" data-step="morning"><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Morning</h3><p>RYZHYI watches the outside world. Warm sunlight reaches the empty sill. No bird has visited; no observation has been saved.</p></div></article>
            <article class="story-step" data-step="bird"><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>The visitor</h3><p>A small bird flies in and lands outside. The scripted world supplies the observation: a bird at <code>world/window/bird-01</code>.</p></div></article>
            <article class="story-step" data-step="model-one"><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>The model wakes</h3><p>A temporary call processes the host-supplied observation: “A bird at the window.” This is a scripted illustration, not an actual LLM call.</p></div></article>
            <article class="story-step" data-step="memory"><span class="step-number">04</span><div><h3>Something remains</h3><p>The trusted host saves the sourced observation. The model call ends. Its memory indicator stays lit outside the call.</p></div></article>
            <article class="story-step" data-step="night"><span class="step-number">05</span><div><h3>Night</h3><p>The bird leaves. Real night arrives outside; the room cools to blue and city windows glow. RYZHYI rests. The saved note remains with the trusted host; no model is running.</p></div></article>
            <article class="story-step" data-step="morning-two"><span class="step-number">06</span><div><h3>Another morning</h3><p>New dawn. The bird returns. A different model call begins, and the trusted host supplies yesterday’s sourced observation. Different model call. Same cat. Continuing history.</p></div></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="story-truth">This is a deterministic illustration, not a live AI execution. The model reasons temporarily. The trusted host owns identity, persistent storage, permissions and authority over external actions. Ginger Tail provides reusable continuity mechanisms; the memory marker is only a visual metaphor.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter get-tail" id="chapter-04" aria-labelledby="get-title">
        <div class="chapter-index"><span>04 / Get your Tail</span><span>Experimental interfaces · v0.1.0</span></div>
        <div class="get-heading">
          <div><p class="overline">Bring your own cat</p><h2 id="get-title">A small engine.<br /><span>Your own life.</span></h2></div>
          <p>Ginger Tail is a Node.js foundation, not a hosted pet. Your trusted host supplies the identity, store, model runner, observations and authority.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="get-grid">
          <div class="install-block">
            <div class="block-label"><span>INSTALL FROM GIT</span><span>NODE 22+</span></div>
            <pre><code>npm install 'git+https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail.git#v0.1.0'</code></pre>
            <p>The package isn't published to npm. Pin a reviewed release; its interfaces are experimental.</p>
            <a class="text-link dark-link" href="https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Read the architecture</span><span class="link-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="example-block">
            <div class="block-label"><span>ONE WAKE, YOUR HOST</span><span>EXAMPLE</span></div>
            <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable runWake code example"><code><span class="code-keyword">import</span> &#123; createFileStore, runWake &#125; <span class="code-keyword">from</span> 'ginger-tail'

<span class="code-keyword">const</span> identity = &#123; id: 'my-cat' &#125;
<span class="code-keyword">const</span> store = createFileStore(&#123;
  directory: './state', agentId: identity.id,
&#125;)

<span class="code-keyword">const</span> result = <span class="code-keyword">await</span> runWake(&#123;
  identity, store,
  world: &#123; observe: <span class="code-keyword">async</span> () =&gt; (&#123; event: 'A bird.' &#125;) &#125;,
  decide: <span class="code-keyword">async</span> () =&gt; (&#123; kind: 'rest' &#125;),
&#125;)</code></pre>
            <p>The host owns persistence, source checks, permissions and effects. The model cannot approve itself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <details class="mochi-details">
          <summary><span>Meet Mochi, the runnable demo</span><span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary>
          <div class="mochi-content">
            <p>One cat, one terminal, persistent local conversation. Offline mode is deterministic, not a pretend LLM. Type “What do you remember?”, try <code>/sleep</code>, then run it again.</p>
            <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Mochi offline demo commands"><code>git clone https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail.git
cd ginger-tail
npm run demo:cat</code></pre>
            <p class="mochi-optional">Want a local model? Install Ollama and a model first:</p>
            <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Mochi Ollama commands"><code>ollama pull llama3.2:3b
CAT_MODEL=llama3.2:3b npm run demo:cat</code></pre>
            <a class="text-link dark-link" href="https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail/blob/main/examples/meet-a-cat.mjs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>See how Mochi works</span><span class="link-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <footer class="site-footer">
          <a class="footer-title" href="https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Give the cat a tail <span aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></a>
          <div class="footer-bottom"><span>Ginger Tail · experimental Node.js runtime · MIT</span><a href="https://github.com/jomko/ginger-tail" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The source is the source <span aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" focusable="false"><path d="M2 10 10 2M4 2h6v6" /></svg></span></a><a href="#chapter-01">Back to the beginning ↑</a></div>
        </footer>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script src="../scripts/story.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
